          "content": {
            "id": "2a89da24-47c7-30d5-9ce0-86605935ee3b",
            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "Kering delays full Valentino acquisition to 2028 amid debt concerns",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "Kering said on Wednesday that it will not fully buy Italian fashion brand Valentino until at least 2028, its first major move under new CEO Luca de Meo, pushing back the execution of an expensive deal that has been weighing on the heavily indebted group.  The deal - announced just a day after de Meo was charged by shareholders to put the struggling Gucci-owner back on track - crosses a first major item off the Italian's to-do list as he seeks to further reduce Kering's 9.5 billion euro ($11.13 billion) debt pile.  Kering's commitment to fully acquire the business from Qatar-backed fund Mayhoola, made in a deal in 2023, has been weighing heavily on the indebted French luxury group whose balance sheet has come under market scrutiny amid declining sales.",
